---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "13 November 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Morph — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Morph, the word ladder game for Mac, iPhone and iPad by DataIsland Software LLC."
>

  <section class="legal fade-in">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/privacy">← All Privacy Policies</a></div>

    <h1>Morph — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">DataIsland Software LLC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      Morph is a word ladder game for Mac, iPhone and iPad in English, French, Spanish and German.
      This policy explains what data Morph uses, what is stored on your device, and what, if
      anything, leaves it.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Morph does not collect personal data and makes no network requests while you play.</strong>
      The word lists and puzzles are built into the app. The app has no server, no account, no ads
      and no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What Is Stored on Your Device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your puzzles</strong>: the words you played, hints used and results, so you can pick a puzzle up again and see your statistics and streaks</li>
      <li><strong>Your choices</strong>: the two languages you picked and your settings</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These are stored in the app's own storage on your device (UserDefaults). They are not synced
      to iCloud and are never sent to DataIsland.
    </p>

    <h2>What Leaves Your Device</h2>

    <h3>Playing: Nothing</h3>
    <p>
      Checking words, making practice puzzles, hints and statistics all run on your device using
      the word lists inside the app.
    </p>

    <h3>Buying the Full Game</h3>
    <p>
      When you buy or restore the Full Game, the purchase is handled entirely by Apple's App Store.
      DataIsland receives no payment details or personal information from Apple about you.
    </p>

    <h3>Sharing a Result</h3>
    <p>
      If you tap Share after a daily puzzle, Morph prepares a short line of text (for example,
      the puzzle number, languages and your rating) and hands it to the system share sheet. Where
      it goes is your choice. Morph sends nothing on its own.
    </p>

    <h2>What Morph Does Not Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Does not transmit any data to DataIsland's servers</li>
      <li>Does not require an account or login</li>
      <li>Does not show ads or track you across apps and websites</li>
      <li>Does not collect analytics or usage statistics</li>
      <li>Does not access your contacts, photos, location, files or microphone</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Morph collects no information from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the "Last updated" date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:<br />
      <a href="mailto:support@dataisland.com">support@dataisland.com</a><br />
      DataIsland Software LLC
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .legal h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .legal h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal p  { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }

  ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
  }

  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
